      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to understand the concept of similar triangles and how their corresponding sides are proportional.\n\n1. **Identify the given information:**\n   - The original isosceles triangle has side lengths 8 cm, 8 cm, and 10 cm.\n   - The longest side of the original triangle is 10 cm.\n   - The longest side of the similar triangle is 25 cm.\n\n2. **Determine the ratio of the corresponding sides:**\n   - The ratio of the longest side of the larger triangle to the longest side of the original triangle is:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{25 \\text{ cm}}{10 \\text{ cm}} = 2.5\n     \\]\n   - This ratio means that each side of the larger triangle is 2.5 times the corresponding side of the original triangle.\n\n3. **Calculate the side lengths of the larger triangle:**\n   - The first side of the larger triangle is:\n     \\[\n     8 \\text{ cm} \\times 2.5 = 20 \\text{ cm}\n     \\]\n   - The second side of the larger triangle is:\n     \\[\n     8 \\text{ cm} \\times 2.5 = 20 \\text{ cm}\n     \\]\n   - The third side of the larger triangle is:\n     \\[\n     10 \\text{ cm} \\times 2.5 = 25 \\text{ cm}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Find the perimeter of the larger triangle:**\n   - The perimeter is the sum of all three sides:\n     \\[\n     20 \\text{ cm} + 20 \\text{ cm} + 25 \\text{ cm} = 65 \\text{ cm}\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the perimeter of the larger triangle is \\(\\boxed{65}\\) centimeters.",
