      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to understand the concept of similar triangles. Two triangles are similar if their corresponding angles are equal and their corresponding sides are proportional. In this case, the ratio of the longest sides of the two triangles is equal to the ratio of their perimeters.\n\nGiven:\n- The side lengths of the first triangle are 8 cm, 8 cm, and 10 cm.\n- The longest side of the first triangle is 10 cm.\n- The longest side of the similar triangle is 25 cm.\n\nWe need to find the perimeter of the larger triangle.\n\nStep 1: Find the ratio of the longest sides of the two triangles.\nThe ratio of the longest sides is \\( \\frac{25}{10} = 2.5 \\).\n\nStep 2: Use this ratio to find the perimeter of the larger triangle.\nSince the ratio of the longest sides is 2.5, the perimeter of the larger triangle will be 2.5 times the perimeter of the smaller triangle.\n\nThe perimeter of the smaller triangle is \\( 8 + 8 + 10 = 26 \\) cm.\nSo, the perimeter of the larger triangle is \\( 2.5 \\times 26 = 65 \\) cm.\n\nLet's verify this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given side lengths of the first triangle\nside1 = 8\nside2 = 8\nside3 = 10\n\n# Longest side of the first triangle\nlongest_side_first_triangle = side3\n\n# Longest side of the similar triangle\nlongest_side_similar_triangle = 25\n\n# Ratio of the longest sides\nratio = longest_side_similar_triangle / longest_side_first_triangle\n\n# Perimeter of the smaller triangle\nperimeter_smaller_triangle = side1 + side2 + side3\n\n# Perimeter of the larger triangle\nperimeter_larger_triangle = ratio * perimeter_smaller_triangle\nprint(perimeter_larger_triangle)\n```\n```output\n65.0\n```\nThe perimeter of the larger triangle is \\(\\boxed{65}\\) centimeters.",
